            <div xml:id="d423">

                <pb facs="0592" n="512" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg512"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.6176/26: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-10-01T12:00:00+01:00">October 1,
                            1936—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received October 1—9:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>451. My 448, September 28, 11 a.m., and previous telegrams. Townsend, who is
                    sailing Saturday, called at the Chancery this morning <pb facs="0593" n="513"
                        xml:id="pg513"/> to say that he thought the Embassy’s representations had
                    had a beneficial effect. The currency situation had naturally made any decision
                    impossible at the recent meeting of the International Rubber Committee, but he
                    personally expected that the October 27 meeting would authorize a further
                    release, probably by 5%, beginning January 1st. I gather he obtained this
                    impression from Campbell.</p>
                <p>Townsend said that he had had satisfactory conversations with his German
                    colleague who felt that the German Government should likewise make
                    representations on behalf of German consumers and he would urge this course on
                    his Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
